@page
@model FullModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Protected project inventory";
}

<section class="page-intro protected-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Protected project inventory</p>
    <h1>Additional project context for approved reviewers.</h1>
    <p>This convenience gate protects fuller career context. It does not include client names, credentials, proprietary workflows, or confidential outcomes.</p>
</section>

@if (!Model.HasAccess)
{
    <section class="access-form">
        @if (!Model.IsConfigured)
        {
            <p class="success-message" role="status">Access is being configured. Please contact Ben for the inventory link and password.</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <form method="post" asp-page-handler="Unlock">
                <div asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly" role="alert"></div>
                <label asp-for="Password">Inventory password <input asp-for="Password" autocomplete="current-password" /></label>
                <button class="button" type="submit">Open inventory</button>
            </form>
        }
    </section>
}
else
{
    <section class="protected-projects" aria-label="Protected project inventory">
        <div class="protected-project">
            <p class="eyebrow">Public sector · Product leadership</p>
            <h2>State public housing department</h2>
            <p>Ben served as Overall Product Owner and lead product person for a multi-year, multi-module transformation. He worked closely with UX and helped develop the backlog and roadmap across capital-project planning, financial submissions, rental-assistance reporting, and an AI-assisted utility-data submission workflow.</p>
            <p class="project-role">ASP.NET · C# · SQL Server · Entity Framework · Azure · Azure Document Intelligence</p>
        </div>
        <div class="protected-project">
            <p class="eyebrow">Legal services · Experience design</p>
            <h2>Top NYC law firm</h2>
            <p>As UX Design Lead and a design-thinking workshop facilitator, Ben shaped Power BI dashboard and client-intelligence portal concepts. The work concluded with a leadership presentation of the proposed implementation roadmap and product backlog; later implementation is not attributed here.</p>
            <p class="project-role">UX leadership · Power BI · Workshops · Roadmap · Backlog</p>
        </div>
        <div class="protected-project">
            <p class="eyebrow">Commercial real estate · Analytics</p>
            <h2>Commercial real-estate reporting</h2>
            <p>Ben designed the experience for a Power BI dashboard supporting accounting and reporting across property data, monthly rent, net operating income, and related measures. He facilitated design-thinking work and collaborated with the team responsible for the data model and warehouse.</p>
            <p class="project-role">Power BI · Dashboard UX · Data modeling collaboration · Design thinking</p>
        </div>
        <div class="protected-project">
            <p class="eyebrow">Nuology · Launched product</p>
            <h2>Launched resale-inventory product</h2>
            <p>ThriftTrack is a launched Nuology product for capturing, searching, editing, and organizing resale inventory on mobile and web. Its product context includes organization-scoped persistence, with mobile and web delivery supported by React Native and Supabase.</p>
            <p class="project-role">Founder work · React Native · TypeScript · Supabase · Mobile · Web</p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <form method="post" asp-page-handler="Lock" class="lock-form"><button class="text-link" type="submit">Close protected inventory</button></form>
}
